            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to impose, then the Marathi for a provision."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: जोपर्यंत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जोपर्यंत — joparyant — \"as long as; until\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जोपर्यंत तू येत नाहीस, मी जेवणार नाही. joparyant tū yet nāhīs, mī jevṇār nāhī. I won't eat until you come."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a negative it means until: जोपर्यंत (joparyant) … नाही; a तो- clause often answers it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जोपर्यंत (joparyant) is built from जो, \"which\", and -पर्यंत, \"up to\", from Sanskrit paryanta, \"limit, edge\" (Monier-Williams): up to the point which."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
