              "text": "जेणेकरून — jeṇekarūn — \"so that\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मी लवकर निघालो, जेणेकरून गाडी चुकू नये. mī lavkar nighālo, jeṇekarūn gāḍī cukū naye. I left early so that I wouldn't miss the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Followed by a should-form or a future: जेणेकरून (jeṇekarūn) … होईल."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जेणेकरून (jeṇekarūn) is built from जेणे, \"by which\", an old instrumental form of the relative जो, \"which\", and करून, \"having done\": done in such a way that. Sanskrit had the same pair, the relative ya- and its instrumental yena (CDIAL 10391)."
            }
          ]
        },
